      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROCKABYE ROXY (5) finally knocked over the maiden last time and looks set to work her way through the grades now. She's been closing nicely from the back of the pack and the rise in trip looks to suit her. Should lob in a midfield position and in a CL1 that lacks depth, she can repeat the dose. TEXAN STAR (8) bumped into one two back at the Sapphire Coast before a 3L defeat at this track last time out. Now rises to 1750m for the first time, but he may be able to dictate proceedings from the front. Can be in this for a very long way. EMPIRE TIME (6) stepped out to 1900m for the first time and showed some improvement, despite being a long way off the winner. Showed enough there however and he's building nicely. Can feature in the finish. BELLA PIAZZA (1) is on the quick turnaround from last weekend, though getting back on top of the ground appears a big tick. MALINGA MISSILE (3) can feature out to this trip for the first time.",
